-- title:
--   Blown-up chart has an end on each component through y
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and assume (`hK`) that $K$ is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H$ for $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ and $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring, a domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), together with a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function, with coefficients pushed from $\mathbb{Q}$ to $L$). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and assume (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves over $\Omega$ have no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart algebra along the two inclusions into the $j$-finite and $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebras, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart package at every supersingular point of the special fibre; its conclusion has seven clauses, summarised below) states: for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ that is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma \varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})\,v - f\,u)$, such that, writing `toC` for the completion map, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$ and `germY` for the composite $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ taking germs at $z$ through the chart $\operatorname{Spec} C$: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $\sigma a$; (ii) every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}(K/L)$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ realises on quotients of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0,H)$ the slash action by `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, compatibly with the embedding normalised by $\xi \mapsto \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ — for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as above acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining the $\tau$-action on germs with $e$, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_k) \equiv \sum_i M_{ik}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal $(X_0,X_1)$ of $S$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ik} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ik}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, with $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ which do not contain both $X_0$ and $X_1$, contain $\sigma\varpi$, and contain elements $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ whose direction vectors satisfy $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above containing $\varpi$ and an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a \in C$, the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ coefficient form $\sum_{i\le e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, such that $e$ sends the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   Next, a specific such point and witness are fixed: a point $z$ of $X$ with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` image $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y' = y$ (`hy'y`), and data $W_1$, $\sigma_1$, $f_1$, $u_1$, $v_1$, $e_1$ as above, for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) just listed.
--
--   The centre of the blow-up is an ideal $J$ of $C$ with (`hJ`) $J$ equal to the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ of $C$ for which there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, and $J'$ equal to the preimage under $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ with (`hB`) $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$, the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Four further groups of hypotheses are imposed. `hR1`: $C \subseteq B$, and every $f \in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$. `hR2`: $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the complement of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, in the sense that $f \in W$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here): first, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) whose kernel consists of the elements of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, which on $A$ is the residue map followed by the structure map, and which is equivariant for the level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, leaving $W$ stable: for each such pair there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the kernel [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) of $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)c^{q+1}$ such that $\rho(\tau b) =$ `hAction` of that element applied to $\rho(b)$, and $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; second, $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; third, every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the image under some level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, of all elements of $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$; fourth, an element of $B$ all of whose images under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; fifth, a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ also preserves $W$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $C$ which is prime, contains the image of $\varpi$, and satisfies $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq y$ and $\mathfrak{p} \ne y$, there exists a subring $O$ of $K$ with the following two properties.
--
--   First, there are an element $a \in J \subseteq C$ whose image in $K$ is nonzero and, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ given by the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ xa = i\}$ (the chart $C[J/a]$ of the blow-up of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ along $J$), a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$, such that: $f \in O$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$, that is, $O$ is the localisation $(B_a)_P$; every element of $y$ whose image lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$; and $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   Second, there is a prime ideal $\mathfrak{q}$ of $O$ such that: the image of $\varpi$, if it lies in $O$, lies in $\mathfrak{q}$; there is an element $b \in y$ whose image, if it lies in $O$, is not in $\mathfrak{q}$; and for every $c \in C$ whose image lies in $O$, one has $c \in \mathfrak{p}$ if and only if that image lies in $\mathfrak{q}$.
--
--   This is the existence statement that each component of the special fibre through the supersingular point $y$ — encoded as a prime $\mathfrak p$ of the chart algebra with $\varpi \in \mathfrak p \subsetneq y$ — carries a point of the blow-up of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ along the weighted centre $J$ which does not lie on the exceptional Drinfeld component cut out by $B$ and $W$, the local ring $O$ at that point contracting to $\mathfrak p$. It is one conjunct of the description of the exceptional fibre of the integral model of the full-level modular curve at a supersingular point, used in the analysis of the components of that fibre.
